        "date": "2026-11-17T06:12:10Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(motion): start the bore dive over the uncut core under carried stock\n\nA bore-side contour cuts only its ring. When the Ramp entry's chord is\nblocked on a later level, the substituted dive lands along the first\npass, a wall margin inward from the cut path. Its footprint then meets\nthe core inside the ring, which stands at the top of the material. The\nold code took the plane above as the material's top there and rapided\ninto carried stock (verify RapidInStock on the second level).\n\nThe bore side now reads the material's top at the dive point: the plane\nabove where the point is on the cut path or an earlier plunge opened\nthat column, else the top of the material. The substituted dive and the\nPlunge arm use it. Later levels keep the short rapid over the plane\nabove, because the first dive opened the column.\n\nFixes #2301\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
